    "https://hr.umn.edu/jobs/Find-Job/Executive-Searches/Vice-Chancellor-Enrollment-Management-Morris": {
      "title": "Breadcrumb",
      "description": "Vice Chancellor for Enrollment Management - Morris | University of Minnesota Office of Human Resources Skip to main content Go to the University of Minnesota Twin Cities home page One Stop MyU : For Students, Faculty, and Staff Search Office of Human Resources Jobs Why the UMN Benefits at UMN Relocation Assistance Find a Job Search UMN Jobs UMN Student Jobs Featured Positions U Services Positions Veterinary Technician Positions Executive Searches Associate Chancellor - Crookston Executive Director of Admissions – UMN Duluth Executive Medical Director - Boynton Health Vice Chancellor for Enrollment Management - UMN Morris Applicant Support Using the Job Application System Application and Interview Guidance UMN Graduate Assistant Job Guidance UMN Undergraduate Student Job Guidance Veteran Employment Guidance Contact Breadcrumb Home Find a Job Executive Searches Vice Chancellor for Enrollment Management - UMN Morris Vice Chancellor for Enrollment Management - Morris Join the University of Minnesota Morris (UMN Morris) leadership team as the vice chancellor for enrollment management. The vice chancellor serves as a strategic leader responsible for advancing the continued vitality of UMN Morris through integrated recruitment, enrollment, and student success strategies. The vice chancellor reports to the UMN Morris chancellor (primary reporting line) and UMN vice president for strategic enrollment management, as part of the enrollment management team across the five UMN campuses. The vice chancellor works collaboratively across the institution to attract, enroll, retain, and graduate students who will thrive in UMN Morris's distinctive academic and community-engaged environment. In an increasingly competitive and rapidly changing higher education landscape, the vice chancellor provides vision, leadership, and innovation in recruitment, financial aid, and data-informed planning. In collaboration with other campus units, such as marketing and communications, athletics, student life, academic affairs, and others, the vice chancellor champions a student-centered approach that connects enrollment management with academic excellence, access, belonging, student achievement, and institutional sustainability. The vice chancellor will be a member of the University-wide strategic enrollment management team and collaborate with colleagues and offices to develop and implement integrated strategies. The successful candidate is a strategic, mission-driven leader who can tell the UMN Morris story, build enrollment and student success strategies grounded in data, and mobilize the campus community to advance the strength and vitality of a distinctive public liberal arts and sciences university. Contact Contact Brad Earney at [email protected] with any questions about the position or location. Learn more about this role at the University Your browser does not support iframes, but you can visit Five Strong Campuses. One Strong State. The University of Minnesota System is one of the most comprehensive in the nation, with offerings to meet the interests of every student and the changing needs of our society. We're proud of our land-grant mission of world-class education, groundbreaking research, and our commitment to partnering with communities in our drive to serve Minnesota. Learn more about the University of Minnesota System. Learn more about our world-class benefits Learn More Expand all Learn More + About UMN Morris UMN Morris is a student-centered public liberal arts college that offers a world-class education in a close-knit community. As part of the University of Minnesota, Morris provides access to top research facilities, nationally ranked study abroad programs, and small class sizes—all at an affordable cost. Located in the welcoming town of Morris, the campus fosters strong connections between students, faculty, and the local community. Learn more about UMN Morris + Responsibilities Serve as an active member of the UMN Morris senior administrative team, providing direction on all aspects of enrollment management Supervise staff in Admissions, Financial Aid, and One Stop Work closely with Financial Aid to leverage financial aid awards in a manner that enhances the overall student body and expands opportunities for timely degree attainment Collaborate with Marketing and Communications to advance student recruitment and retention efforts Articulate and amplify the distinctive value of a public liberal arts and sciences education, while building pathways for students from rural communities, tribal nations, transfer institutions, and other key populations Align recruitment, financial aid, and retention efforts into a cohesive strategy, with attention to overall student success Oversee successful implementation of strategic enrollment management plan components Create strategies and initiatives that effectively support the recruitment and retention of a diverse and inclusive student body in alignment with the University’s strategic plan, UMN Morris strategic plan, and UMN Morris strategic enrollment management plan Lead the institution's strategy for attracting, supporting, and graduating students in ways that sustain and advance the mission of a rural public liberal arts and sciences University Exhibit and promote data-driven decision-making at the institutional and college levels in collaboration with campus-wide efforts regarding institutional effectiveness and student success Serve as an active contributor to campus governance committees and represent the institution at relevant University meetings Participate in University enrollment management leadership meetings and contribute expertise to advance overall UMN goals and priorities Other responsibilities as assigned, consistent with the role + Qualifications Master's degree (doctoral degree preferred) Demonstrated ability to develop innovative enrollment strategies in response to changing demographics, student needs, and higher education market conditions, with experience or understanding the rural community context Demonstrated ability to use data and institutional research to inform strategic planning, enrollment management, student success initiatives, and organizational decision-making Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the mission and value of public liberal arts education and student-centered learning Demonstrated success building collaborative partnerships across academic and administrative units to achieve institutional goals Proven experience leading and developing high-performing teams while fostering a culture of accountability, innovation, and continuous improvement Exceptional communication, relationship-building, and presentation skills, with the ability to engage effectively with diverse internal and external stakeholders Demonstrated commitment to fostering access, belonging, and student success for individuals from diverse backgrounds and experiences Progressive leadership experience in enrollment management, student success, institutional research, or related areas within higher education + Salary, Benefits, and Other Details Starting salary range: $120,000–142,000 Work arrangements: In person Benefits: As a Professional and Administrative (P&A) employee, you’ll enjoy a comprehensive benefits package with low-cost health coverage, professional development opportunities, and retirement plan with 10% employer contribution. (See our benefits page for more information.) + Applications and Nominations Please submit both a cover letter and a resume (or CV). Apply here The position will remain open until filled. Coming in as a candidate for a position through the executive search process, and having led executive searches in past organizations, my own bar was fairly high. Questions were handled professionally and compassionately. The candidate experience overall was positive and affirming, and I felt I was in good hands throughout. -Autumn Amadou-Blegen, SPHR, SHRM-SCP Associate Vice Chancellor of Human Resources 2026 Best Employers for Company Culture, Forbes 80% Would recommend to a friend, Glassdoor #4 Best States, U.S. News An Equal Opportunity Employer The University of Minnesota shall provide equal access to and opportunity in its programs, facilities, and employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, national origin, gender, age, marital status, disability, public assistance status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression. Talent Acquisition | UMN Office of Human Resources Contact Email: [email protected] Student Employment Email: [email protected] Quick Links Find a Job Comprehensive Benefits Using the Application System This unit has systemwide responsibilities. Learn more about the University of Minnesota System . For Students, Faculty, and Staff One Stop MyU : For Students, Faculty, and Staff © 2026 Regents of the University of Minnesota . All rights reserved. The University of Minnesota is an equal opportunity educator and employer. Privacy Statement Report Web Accessibility Issues Benefits Benefits Enrollment and Changes Enrollment Overview Upcoming Benefits Changes How to Enroll New Employee or Newly Eligible Enrollment Open Enrollment Life Events Reclassification Year-Round Changes Leaving the UMN Leaving the UMN Overview Layoff Severance & Non-Renewal COBRA Continuation of Coverage Preparing for Retirement Medical Benefits Medical Plans Medica Plan Options Pharmacy Program Medication Therapy Management Convenience Care/Walk-in Clinics Virtual Care Travel Program Emergency Travel Program Diabetes Prevention & Management Dental Benefits Dental Plans Dental Plan Availability and Comparison Life and Disability Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance Short-Term Disability Insurance Academic Disability Basic Life Insurance Additional Life Insurance Retirement Savings & Financial Counseling Retirement Savings Plans Overview Plan Comparison Financial Counseling and Resources 